# ludic.furniture - what fills a room a player owns: furniture kinds are rows, an interior is an instance
# the game names by a key (it is the game's property, or a flat, or a cabin; this module never says), and
# what is placed in it is checked and kept per key. The room's size and its own geometry are asked of the
# game through a port; money is a port; what happened is a fact.
module ludic_furniture uses ludic_base
numbers float
import "ludic.base"
import "defs.ludic"
import "state.ludic"
import "geom.ludic"
import "check.ludic"
import "verbs.ludic"
import "query.ludic"
import "system.ludic"
